# Both targets must still be legal for the whole effect: Bot1 targets Bot2 and its Lotus Petal, then sacrifices the Petal for mana in
# response (a mana ability, with the Offering on the stack), so the permanent target is illegal when the spell resolves (CR 608.2b)
# and there is nothing to give: the spell resolves without taking anything from Bot1 or giving Bot2 anything, and the rest of the
# Moxes stay with Bot1.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Harmless Offering
Lotus Petal
Swamp
Swamp
10 Swamp

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Island
Island
Island
Island
Island
Island
10 Island

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Lotus Petal.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Harmless Offering.Cast
Bot1.Target(Bot2)
Bot1.Target(Lotus Petal)
? Stack.Count = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Lotus Petal.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Jet; Mox Ruby; Mox Pearl
Bot1.Graveyard = Harmless Offering; Lotus Petal
